        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "11f26885-333a-5d1f-893d-62a8d2d004b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ferrari 360, Ferrari F355, Porsche 911, Lamborghini Diablo, Mitsubishi Lancer, Subaru Impreza, HSV\n- Organizations: Ferrari, PROCAR\n- Events: Australian Nations Cup Championship, Australian GT Production Car Championship\n\nFacts:\n- The Ferrari F355, also called Type F129, is a sports car that Ferrari built from May 1994 to 1999.\n- In 1999, Ferrari ended production of the Ferrari F355.\n- The Ferrari 360 is a two-seater sports car that Ferrari built from 1999 to 2005.\n- In 2000, PROCAR split the Australian GT Production Car Championship into two separate series.\n- In 2000, Porsche 911s, Ferrari 360s, and Lamborghini Diablos became eligible to compete in the new Australian Nations Cup Championship.\n- In 2000, Mitsubishi Lancers, Subaru Imprezas, and HSV vehicles competed for outright wins in the revised Australian GT Production Car Championship.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b9687d56-963a-59f1-a275-702b523ce11c",
        "text": "Page: Ferrari 360. Sentence: The Ferrari 360 is a two-seater sports car built by Ferrari from 1999 to 2005.\nPage: Ferrari F355. Sentence: The Ferrari F355 (Type F129) is a sports car built by Ferrari from May 1994 to 1999.\nPage: Australian Nations Cup Championship. Sentence: For 2000, PROCAR split the Australian GT Production Car Championship into two separate series so that the more exotic GT cars such as Porsche 911s, Ferrari 360s and Lamborghini Diablo's could compete in the new Australian Nations Cup Championship and the lesser vehicles such as the Mitsubishi Lancers, Subaru Imprezas and HSV's could now compete for outright wins in the revised Australian GT Production Car Championship.",
